          "SEO social network",
          "audit sharing",
          "Traffic Torch profiles",
          "SEO points",
          "SEO community"
        ],
        "wordCount": 2400,
        "inLanguage": "en",
        "articleSection": "Help Guides",
        "isPartOf": {
          "@type": "Blog",
          "name": "Traffic Torch Blog",
          "url": "https://traffictorch.net/news/"
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@id": "https://traffictorch.net/blog/posts/social-help-guide/#faq",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "What is a torch on Traffic Torch?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "A torch is a public audit result you choose to share. Every tool run produces a 0–100 score and a per-module breakdown. When you click 'Post to Community', that audit becomes a torch with its own page at /torch/:id/, a share image, and a permanent link you can send to anyone."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Do I need an account to view the community?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "No. The community feed at /community/, the leaderboard at /leader-board/, every profile at /torcher/:username/, and every torch page at /torch/:id/ are all fully public. You only need an account to post a torch, leave a comment, or add someone to your network."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do I earn points on Traffic Torch?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Points come from four actions: posting a torch (+10), leaving a comment (+5), joining the leaderboard with a shared audit (+10), and submitting a bug report, feature idea, or docs contribution (+25). Points are additive and permanent. They appear next to your name everywhere on the site and rank you on the leaderboard's top contributors section."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How does the leaderboard work?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "The leaderboard at /leader-board/ ranks every audit that a user has explicitly submitted. You can filter by tool, view the top 3 podium, browse the top 12 hall of fame, and see the top contributors by points earned. When a URL is re-audited, the higher of the two scores is kept."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can I hide my domain from the torch or community?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes. When you post a torch you can choose to hide the domain, show it as-is, or show only the domain without the full path. Hidden torches still get a /torch/:id/ page and are still shareable, but they are marked noindex and the domain is masked on the page itself."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do I connect with other SEOs?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Click '+ Add to Network' on any torch page, profile page, or comment. Both users' profiles then appear in each other's Network list, and you both get a notification. You can search for users by name or username at /dashboard/ → Network → Find People."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Is there an RSS feed?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes. There are three: a global feed of all torches at /torches/feed.xml, a per-user feed at /torcher/:username/feed.xml, and a per-tool feed at /tools/:tool/torches/feed.xml. Subscribe in any feed reader to get new torches as they're posted."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

